# TopFlow Hub uses one environment file per application:
#
#   apps/api/.env            → copy from apps/api/.env.example    (database, Supabase, internal secret, mail, company details)
#   apps/web/.env.local      → copy from apps/web/.env.example    (Supabase URL + publishable key, API origin, internal secret)
#   apps/mobile/.env         → copy from apps/mobile/.env.example (API, web and Supabase URLs, publishable key)
#   packages/database/.env   → copy from packages/database/.env.example (database, plus Supabase keys so the seed creates sign-ins)
#
# `npm run supabase:start` starts Supabase locally; `npx supabase status` prints its URLs and keys.
# `npm run setup` creates the API, web and database files from their examples, fills in the local keys
# and a shared INTERNAL_API_SECRET where they are empty, and loads the demo data into the local database.
#
# Seed options (npm run db:seed):
#   SEED_DEMO_PASSWORD=...        password of the demo sign-ins (the default is public: never use it in production)
#   SEED_RESET_PASSWORDS=true     also reset the password of demo identities that already exist
#   SEED_DEMO_DOCUMENTS=false     skip the sample RFQs, quotations and orders
#   SEED_KEEP_UNLISTED=true       leave products that are not in the catalogue file published
#   SEED_FORCE=true               required to seed when NODE_ENV=production
#
# Public demo only (docs/OPERATIONS.md, section 10): `DEMO_MODE=true npm run demo:reset -- --confirm`
# empties the demo database and seeds it again. It refuses a database with accounts but no demo data.
